# Files that must not become public URLs if this is ever deployed via Workers.
# Same syntax as .gitignore. Wrangler skips anything matching these lines when
# it uploads static assets.
#
# THIS FILE IS INERT TODAY. The board is deployed on Cloudflare Pages, which has
# no equivalent ignore file — it uploads the whole output directory. Nothing here
# is protecting anything right now.
#
# What actually gates these files is Cloudflare Access, which sits in front of
# the entire hostname: every path, including the ones below, 302s to the Access
# login unless you are on the policy. Verified 2026-08-01.
#
# This file and wrangler.jsonc are kept together so a future move to Workers
# (Cloudflare's stated direction) does not have to rediscover the list.

# Documentation and planning — not part of the app.
README.md
account-board-implementation-plan.md

# The Firebase rules are pasted into the Firebase console by hand. Serving them
# is not a credential leak (rules are not secret) but it hands a reader the
# exact shape of the database for free.
database.rules.json

# Screenshots kept in the repo for reference — including the two screenshot
# files, which are only for the README. logo.png is different: it is the favicon
# and the wordmark, and the site breaks without it.
*.png
!logo.png

# Deploy config and repo metadata.
wrangler.jsonc
.gitignore
.assetsignore
